%% Zero-downtime cluster upgrade of the stateless clusters: one zonal cluster at a time is drained from the
%% traffic layer, upgraded (or rebuilt), verified and put back. Same pipeline runs in dev, then acc, then prd.
sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    participant P as Upgrade pipeline<br/>(or Fleet Manager update run)
    participant T as Traffic layer<br/>(App Gateway / Front Door)
    participant A as aks-env-sl-az1
    participant B as aks-env-sl-az2
    Note over A,B: Both clusters serve traffic. Each is sized to carry 100 % of the load alone (N+1).
    P->>B: Pre-scale: raise HPA minReplicas / node count to full-load capacity
    P->>T: Set az1 backend weight to 0 (or disable backend)
    T-->>A: Connection draining (no new requests)
    P->>A: Upgrade control plane + node pools<br/>(or create new cluster from IaC, Flux bootstraps it)
    A->>A: Flux reconciles all apps, health checks
    P->>A: Smoke + synthetic tests through cluster-local ingress
    P->>T: Restore az1 weight (gradually, e.g. 10 % → 50 % → 100 %)
    Note over P: Watch error rate / latency SLO. Breach → weight 0 again, stop.
    P->>A: Pre-scale az1, then repeat steps 2–7 for az2 (and az3)
    P->>B: Remove pre-scale, autoscalers take over
